# Variables and conditions
@scenario tutorial_lesson_07
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char ginger global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/07_variables_and_conditions.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt unset]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: A flag is useful when a later line depends on something that already happened. This example resets {b}example_ready{/b} to false each time you start it.
# region unset
[set example_ready false]
[if !example_ready]
ginger: First check. The flag is false.
[endif]
# endregion
[set tutorial_excerpt flag]
# region flag
[flag example_ready]
[if example_ready]
ginger: Second check. The flag is true.
[endif]
# endregion
ginger: Open this script and compare the two if blocks. The exclamation mark reverses the result of the check.
ginger: Remove the flag command and replay. You should still see the first check. The second message should disappear. Restore the command and test again.
ginger: Read each condition with the value it sees at that instant. The first check runs after setting false. The second runs after flag changes the stored value to true.
ginger: A comparison can also depend on a number. At a threshold of two, the difference between greater-than and greater-than-or-equal is visible at exactly one boundary value.
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Test a threshold -> practice
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
ginger: What stores the value between the two checks?
> A story variable. -> correct
> A label name. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide sad]
ginger: A label names a location in the script. The if blocks read a value from the current VN state.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: The story variable holds the value until a later command changes it.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
[if !tutorial_done_07]
[flag tutorial_done_07]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_1]
[end]

@label practice
[show ginger beside_code thoughtful]
[set tutorial_source scripts/tutorial/07_variables_and_conditions.vns]
[set tutorial_excerpt threshold]
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
ginger: Try a numeric condition in the live example. It assigns a score, then adds one before evaluating a threshold. Read those instructions in execution order.
ginger: Write down three cases for a threshold of two. A score of one should miss, two should pass and three should pass. The middle case distinguishes the two comparison operators.
ginger: Start each run from a known score. If a second replay starts one point higher than the first, you are testing leftover state as well as the condition.
ginger: Change the operator from >= to > in the exercise and replay. Watch the value printed by the script alongside the branch it takes.
@label practice_question
ginger: The score starts at one, increases once, and the test is score >= 2. Which path should run?
> The passing path at exactly two. -> practice_result
> The failing path until three. -> practice_hint
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label practice_hint
ginger: Trace the increment before evaluating the condition. Then check whether the comparison includes equality.
[jump practice_question]
@label practice_result
ginger: After the increment, the score is two. Equality satisfies the original comparison. Repeat with the stricter operator and the same initial value.
# region threshold
[set lab_score 1]
@label apply_threshold
[inc lab_score]
[if lab_score >= 2]
ginger: Score ${lab_score}. The comparison passed.
[else]
ginger: Score ${lab_score}. The comparison failed.
[endif]
# endregion
[clear ui.dialogueFacet]
> Test another starting score -> pick_score
> Review question -> check
> Try the exercise again -> practice
> Back to topics -> return_hub

@label pick_score
> Start at zero -> score_zero
> Start at one -> score_one
> Start at two -> score_two
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label score_zero
[set lab_score 0]
[jump show_threshold]
@label score_one
[set lab_score 1]
[jump show_threshold]
@label score_two
[set lab_score 2]
@label show_threshold
[set ui.dialogueFacet tutorial_code]
[jump apply_threshold]
